orgeous art i mean it's a very lyrical  and poetic movie  in a lot of ways and it has that sort of  life and somewhat  melancholic but still beautiful essence  that a lot of those new wave  movies had and it you know sort of goes  until it it reaches a a place where it  seems appropriate to trail off  um but it's just so gorgeous to look at  there's a lot of really varied art  um and from what i've heard again about  this particular film is the art is also  a departure from his older stuff  in the sense that to me it struck me as  being a lot more impressionistic  there are a lot of um backgrounds and  things that almost look like oil  paintings or watercolor paintings in  some places  the animation feels older it's not quite  as you know  modern and from the little i know about  the process of animation it almost  looked like it was authentically hand  drawn  just from the jitters things would have  um  in certain shots you know where people  would have drawn frames  ever so slightly differently the film  has a very sort of multicultural flavor  to it definitely a lot of it takes place  in japan  but um over the course of the story uh  jiro the the main character does visit a  number of  uh other places you know germany and and  some other parts of europe um and the  music especially accentuates this  a lot of the music feels sort of french  or or italian  um and actually shiro's sort of  inspiration and and his hero is an  italian aeronautical engineer  um so there is sort of a multicultural  quality  to this and which which kind of further  at least for me  sort of reminded me of those old new way  films in the 60s  but um it's a gorgeous film it's it's  a it's wonderful to behold um if you can  see it  i'd say definitely check it out um you i  can't imagine you'd be disappointed it's  not a really out there fantasy or  anything like that  um it's certainly a departure uh but it  is  you know it's an opus uh and it's  definitely worth checking out if you're  a movie fan in general like i don't  think that this is  the type of thing you have to be into  anime  to enjoy so uh yeah that's that's my two  cents  um i'm interested to hear what you guys  thought about the movie if you have  uh seen it and uh what uh what's your  favorite miyazaki film  you know this is a a filmmaker i  definitely want to  you know learn more about and uh  whose work i you know i want to check  out more of  so um yeah go see it man  uh hi omiyazaki the wind rises and i  will catch you guys later  cheers
 

